# Initial Setup's Motor Test page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigMotorTest.cs.
#
# The claim: Activate counts the motors from the frame and builds one button per motor, lettered
# A, B, C... in test order and labelled from APMotorLayout.json (ConfigMotorTest.cs:43-109,
# 111-261); each button is testMotor - MAV_CMD_DO_MOTOR_TEST with the motor, the throttle as a
# percentage, the throttle box, the duration box and a motor count (:305-327) - and the vehicle
# acknowledges each one. A motor button sends its own number and no count (:290-303), Test all in
# Sequence sends motor 1 with the count (:274-280), Stop all motors every motor at zero for zero
# seconds (:282-288), and Test all motors every motor in turn (:263-272). The proof is what the
# page sent (config.motortest.last.*, .commands), what the link's retrying request ended with
# (.outcomes), the vehicle's own COMMAND_ACK lines since the press (.ack, .acks), and, for one test
# long enough to catch, the vehicle's motor outputs (.outputs, SERVO_OUTPUT_RAW). The Set Motor
# Spin Arm button's write of MOT_SPIN_ARM is proved by the vehicle's echo, and put back.
#
# SITL is a simulator: it has no propellers and nothing here can hurt anyone. On a real vehicle the
# page's own note applies - "NOTE: PLEASE HOLD DOWN YOUR UAV" (ConfigMotorTest.resx label2) - and
# the propellers come off before any motor is spun. This script is for SITL only.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm, which sets
# FRAME_CLASS 1 (Quad) and FRAME_TYPE 0 (Plus); MOT_SPIN_ARM is the firmware's 0.1. ArduCopter
# runs a motor test disarmed, landed and with the radio calibrated (motor_test.cpp,
# mavlink_motor_control_check), which SITL at rest is. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-motortest.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
#
# A run that stops half way can leave MOT_SPIN_ARM at 0.07; the Spin Arm expectations then fail
# until it is set back to 0.1, by hand or by a fresh SITL.

screen params
window 1600x1200
settle 6

# Initial Setup lists the page once every parameter is in (isConnected && gotAllParams,
# InitialSetup.cs:315-318), and here parameters are downloaded when asked for.
click param-download
settle 15
expect params.held > 1000
expect params.value.FRAME_CLASS 1
expect params.value.FRAME_TYPE 0
expect params.value.MOT_SPIN_ARM 0.1

click tab-setup
expect config.motortest.active false
# Motor Test is an Optional Hardware entry of InitialSetup's list.
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
click setup-page-ConfigMotorTest
settle 2
expect setup.page ConfigMotorTest
expect config.motortest.active true
expect config.motortest.enabled true

# What Activate built. A quad plus has four motors in APMotorLayout.json; it tests motor 3 first,
# then 1, 4 and 2, so button A is labelled with motor 3.
expect config.motortest.count 4
expect config.motortest.letters A,B,C,D
expect config.motortest.buttons Test motor A,Test motor B,Test motor C,Test motor D
expect config.motortest.labels A=Motor Number: 3, CW;B=Motor Number: 1, CCW;C=Motor Number: 4, CW;D=Motor Number: 2, CCW
expect config.motortest.class Class: Quad
expect config.motortest.type Type: Plus
# The Designer's values: throttle 5 %, duration 2 s.
expect config.motortest.throttle 5
expect config.motortest.duration 2
expect config.motortest.press none
expect config.motortest.link ~ connect-escs-and-motors.html

# Test motor A: DO_MOTOR_TEST motor 1, throttle type 0 (percent), 5 %, 2 s, count 0.
click motortest-motor-A
settle 1
expect config.motortest.press Test motor A
expect config.motortest.last.params 1 0 5 2 0 0 0
expect config.motortest.commands 1/5/2/0
expect config.motortest.outcomes accepted
expect config.motortest.ack MAV_CMD_DO_MOTOR_TEST: accepted
expect config.motortest.acks 1
# Let the vehicle's two seconds run out.
settle 3

# Test all in Sequence: motor 1 with the count, 4.
click motortest-sequence
settle 1
expect config.motortest.press Test all in Sequence
expect config.motortest.last.params 1 0 5 2 4 0 0
expect config.motortest.outcomes accepted
expect config.motortest.ack MAV_CMD_DO_MOTOR_TEST: accepted
expect config.motortest.acks 1

# Stop all motors, with the sequence still running: every motor, zero throttle, zero seconds, and
# the vehicle acknowledges all four.
click motortest-stop
settle 2
expect config.motortest.press Stop all motors
expect config.motortest.commands 1/0/0/0,2/0/0/0,3/0/0/0,4/0/0/0
expect config.motortest.last.params 4 0 0 0 0 0 0
expect config.motortest.outcomes accepted,accepted,accepted,accepted
expect config.motortest.acks 4
expect config.motortest.ack MAV_CMD_DO_MOTOR_TEST: accepted

# The duration box takes a typed number, read when a button reads it. Ten seconds is long enough
# to see the motor turn: Test motor B is motor 1, output 1, at 5 % of SITL's 1000-2000 range.
click motortest-duration
key ctrl+u
type 10
expect config.motortest.duration 10
click motortest-motor-B
settle 2
expect config.motortest.last.params 2 0 5 10 0 0 0
expect config.motortest.outcomes accepted
expect config.motortest.outputs 1050,1000,1000,1000
click motortest-stop
settle 2
expect config.motortest.outcomes accepted,accepted,accepted,accepted

# The arrows step by one: back to 2 s, then Test all motors, every motor in turn.
click motortest-duration
key ctrl+u
type 3
click motortest-duration-down
expect config.motortest.duration 2
click motortest-all
settle 2
expect config.motortest.press Test all motors
expect config.motortest.commands 1/5/2/0,2/5/2/0,3/5/2/0,4/5/2/0
expect config.motortest.outcomes accepted,accepted,accepted,accepted
expect config.motortest.acks 4
click motortest-stop
settle 2
expect config.motortest.outcomes accepted,accepted,accepted,accepted

# Set Motor Spin Arm: the throttle is under 20, so the InputBox asks for it plus 2, and OK writes
# 7 / 100 to MOT_SPIN_ARM; the vehicle echoes it and the page is enabled again (:341-367).
click motortest-spin-arm
expect config.motortest.enabled false
expect config.motortest.prompt Enter arm throttle % (deadzone + 2%)
expect config.motortest.prompt.value 7
click motortest-prompt-ok
settle 2
expect config.motortest.prompt none
expect config.motortest.spin MOT_SPIN_ARM 0.07 accepted
expect params.value.MOT_SPIN_ARM 0.07
expect config.motortest.enabled true

# And back to 0.1: 10 typed over the 7.
click motortest-spin-arm
key ctrl+u
type 10
click motortest-prompt-ok
settle 2
expect config.motortest.spin MOT_SPIN_ARM 0.1 accepted
expect params.value.MOT_SPIN_ARM 0.1

# Set Motor Spin Min asks for (int)MOT_SPIN_MIN + 3: the fraction truncates, so 3. Cancel writes
# nothing and enables the page.
click motortest-spin-min
expect config.motortest.prompt Enter min spin throttle % (arm min + 3%)
expect config.motortest.prompt.value 3
click motortest-prompt-cancel
expect config.motortest.prompt none
expect config.motortest.enabled true

# Choosing another page hides this one; ConfigMotorTest has no Deactivate.
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
settle 1
expect config.motortest.active false
